---
id: staged-review
title: Produce, review, approve
purpose: A known route with a review step; one agent produces a draft, a second agent reviews it, a human approves.
use_when: The route is known and nothing should be accepted before an independent review and a human decision.
produces: The text outputs `produce.draft` and `review.review_notes`, then one REVIEW Human Task at `approve`. Approving it accepts the mission.
slots:
  application_id:
    description: This server's application id (the start page names it).
    example: demo-app
  mission_key:
    description: "A stable slug for the mission: lower case letters, digits, `-` or `_`."
    example: staged-review
  title:
    description: A one-line title.
    example: A reviewed one-page brief
  goal:
    description: What to produce, for whom and in which form, one line.
    example: Write a one-page brief on how a Stage Graph releases its stages.
  criterion:
    description: How the reviewer knows it is done, one line.
    example: The brief is accurate, fits one page and the review found no open defect.
  model_profile:
    description: The producer's Model Profile (topic `models`).
    example: producer.default
  reviewer_model_profile:
    description: The reviewing agent's Model Profile; prefer another vendor than the producer's.
    example: judge.default
  sandbox_profile:
    description: A sandbox profile bound on this installation (topic `manifest`).
    example: research.standard
  budget_usd:
    description: The ceiling on model spend in US dollars, a number.
    example: "1"
  reviewer:
    description: Who resolves the approval; an actor id, or a reviewer role such as `owner`. Only that actor, or a principal holding `reviewer:<role>`, can.
    example: owner
notes:
  - The `review` stage reads the accepted draft through its `from` binding. A start is refused with `dependent_inputs_unavailable` where the installation composes no trusted settlement to accept the draft.
  - Each stage may only narrow the mission budget; the two stage budgets here sum under it.
---
manifest: mission/v2
mission:
  key: {{mission_key}}
  application: {{application_id}}
  title: >-
    {{title}}
  description: >-
    {{goal}}
  goals:
    - key: deliverable
      description: >-
        {{goal}}
      importance: primary
      objectives:
        - key: produce_draft
          description: Produce the draft and submit it as the output named draft.
        - key: review_draft
          description: Review the accepted draft against the goal and submit the findings as review_notes.
      criteria:
        - key: approved
          description: >-
            {{criterion}}
          evidence: [draft, review_notes]
          acceptance:
            human: review_accept
  environment:
    lane: deep_agents
    model:
      profile: {{model_profile}}
    sandbox:
      profile: {{sandbox_profile}}
    capabilities:
      - pin: tool.knowledge-submit-output@latest
        kind: tool
        as: submit_output
    budget:
      usd: {{budget_usd}}
      tokens: 400000
      wall_clock: 45m
      tool_calls: 30
    governors:
      depth: 1
      fan_out: 1
      iterations: 1
      patience: 1
    side_effects: [read_only, workspace_write]
  program:
    key: root
    behavior: stage_graph
    objectives: [deliverable]
    nodes:
      - key: produce
        behavior: agent_executor
        objectives: [produce_draft]
        environment:
          budget:
            tokens: 200000
            tool_calls: 15
        instruction: >-
          {{goal}}
          Submit the draft with the submit_output tool: one call, obligation "produce.draft",
          one inline text item. Stop after its receipt.
        outputs:
          - name: draft
            form: text
            media_type: text/plain
      - key: review
        behavior: agent_executor
        objectives: [review_draft]
        environment:
          model:
            profile: {{reviewer_model_profile}}
          budget:
            tokens: 150000
            tool_calls: 12
        inputs:
          - name: draft
            from: produce.draft
            expand: materialize
        instruction: >-
          Review the draft you received as the input named draft against this goal: {{goal}}
          List each defect with the passage it concerns, or state that you found none.
          Submit the findings with the submit_output tool: one call, obligation
          "review.review_notes", one inline text item. Stop after its receipt.
        outputs:
          - name: review_notes
            form: text
            media_type: text/plain
      - key: approve
        behavior: human_gate
        objectives: [deliverable]
        depends_on: [review]
        task:
          kind: REVIEW
          prompt: >-
            {{criterion}}
          reviewers: [{{reviewer}}]
          packet: [produce.draft, review.review_notes]
          on_timeout: keep_waiting
  controls:
    commands_allowed: [pause, resume, cancel, queue_instruction, add_context]
